d. not employing Children at night; working hours of a maximum of (three) hours per day; f. not being employed in a place or environment that can interfere with the Child's growth and development process, whether physically, mentally, morally and intellectually or the Child's health;
g. providing opportunities to obtain education in accordance with their talents and interests;
h. employing for light types of work; and i. providing one day off per week.

