a. Children who become refugees;

Children who are victims of unrest;

Children who are victims of natural disasters; and Children in armed conflict situations.

Article 170

Special Protection for Children in emergency situations who become refugees as referred to in Article 169 letter is carried out with the following provisions:
a. b. for Children who become refugees is implemented in accordance with humanitarian law provisions;

for Children who are victims of unrest, victims of natural disasters, and Children in armed conflict situations as referred to in Article 169 letter b, letterc, and letter d, is implemented through:

1. fulfillment of basic needs consisting of food, clothing, housing, education, health, learning and recreation, security guarantees, and equal treatment; and fulfillment of special needs for Children with disabilities and Children experiencing psychosocial disorders.

Paragraph Children in Conflict with the Law

